    "body": "Hmm, with cargo registry this is a clear win but homebrew builds things on their own so you don't get much by requiring a successful build (which is a prerequisite of a successful Github release). At best you'll gonna prevent that one PR that's going to fail on their end anyway. I mean it is not an objection just an observation :shrug:\n\nThis is definitely a step in the right direction but we need to ensure that both test suite and build go green before publishing releases. If I'm reading our manifests right, currently there is a chance (unlikely though) of distributing the release that compiles successfully but fails to pass all our tests?\n\nAll in all, LGTM",
